*.log
logs/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.pid

# ─── Audio, video, and model weights ─────────────────────────
# NOTHING that carries a voice belongs in this repository. The clips this project clones from are
# recordings of somebody's voice - the user's own, in the case it was built around - and that is
# not the repository's business either way. A sample committed once stays in the history for good.
#
# The rule used to be `*.mp3` alone, which was the one format the project never produced: every
# reference clip it actually uses is a .wav (mono 24 kHz, cut to 3-10 s) and the kikivoice clone
# sample is whatever ffmpeg read, usually .m4a. So the guard covered the format nobody had and
# missed both of the ones everybody does. Extensions, not paths, because the samples are kept
# outside the tree on purpose and this only has to catch the day somebody forgets.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.flac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.aac
*.wma
*.mka
*.mkv
*.mp4
*.m4v
*.mov
*.webm
*.eac3
*.ac3
*.dts
*.srt
*.ass
*.vtt
# Model checkpoints: gigabytes, and none of them are ours to redistribute.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.gguf

# ─── lektor-ai ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything a run writes beside the episode: subtitles, the script, the cache, the finished
# track. Reproducible from the source and the config, and measured in hundreds of megabytes.
_lektor/
.zrodla/

# The working copy: paths, which engine, whose voice. Template: lektor.toml.example
/lektor.toml

# Written by tools/bench_condense.py on every run, from whatever lektor.toml says.
/tools/bench_cfg.json
